DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: MoTA Museum of Transitory Art: Production Residency 2027 
 (Ljubljana)
DESCRIPTION:MoTA (Museum of Transitory Art) in Ljubljana runs an annual ope
 n call for production residencies for media\, sound and visual artists\, c
 urators and researchers. Production residencies offer full support includi
 ng accommodation\, technical support\, production costs and an artist fee\
 ; the exact artist-fee amount is not published on the official or aggregat
 or pages\, so applicants should confirm the figure directly by email. Resi
 dencies run up to one month. Open internationally: artists of all national
 ities and at all professional levels are encouraged to apply\, as individu
 als or collectives. No application fee. The annual deadline is 15 Septembe
 r (for residencies the following year). Apply by email to mota.artists@gma
 il.com with the subject line Application for production residency. Note: t
 he official motamuseum.com SSL certificate is currently expired\, which ma
 y briefly affect link reliability.\n\nOrganisation: MoTA - Museum of Trans
 itory Art\nLocation: Ljubljana\, Slovenia. Open internationally to artists
  of all nationalities and professional levels.\nAward: Full support includ
 ing accommodation\, technical support\, production costs and an artist fee
 . The exact EUR artist-fee amount is not published\; confirm by email. No 
 application fee.\nDuration: Production residency of up to one month.\n\nMo
 re: http://motamuseum.com/RESIDENCY/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:http://motamuseum.com/RESIDENCY/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Ljubljana\, Slovenia. Open internationally to artists of all natio
 nalities and professional levels.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:q-o2-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Q-O2: Residency Programme 2027 (Experimental Music & Soun
 d Art)
DESCRIPTION:The residencies at Q-O2 offer time and space for artistic resea
 rch\, reflection and creation in the field of experimental music and sound
  art. In 2027\, Q-O2 will host 20 residencies\, 10 for international artis
 ts and 10 for local artists living in Belgium\, working with\, on or aroun
 d sound. The programme is open to artists\, art workers and theorists who 
 wish to pursue a research-oriented project\; note that Q-O2 does not organ
 ise production-directed residencies and is not a rehearsal space. Duos are
  possible\, and exceptionally small groups too. SUPPORT: a work studio and
  materials\, a creative and communicative environment\, and the possibilit
 y to present work to a public and/or propose a workshop\; for internationa
 l residents\, accommodation in a shared apartment and a contribution to tr
 avel expenses of up to EUR 200\; and a small subsistence budget reserved f
 or artists who do not come with other funding. There is no artist fee. A f
 inal public presentation can be arranged if the artist wishes but is not e
 xpected\; what Q-O2 requires are some traces of the residency in word\, im
 age and/or audio form. APPLY by 15 September 2026: email a concise project
  proposal of no more than one page plus a permanent link to your website o
 r other secondary information (no temporary links) to info@q-o2.be with th
 e subject 'Residency27 - your name'. State where you would travel from\, h
 ow long you would like to stay (4 to 6 weeks)\, and your interest in Q-O2 
 as a working environment\, and make sure you receive an email confirmation
  of receipt.\n\nOrganisation: Q-O2 (workspace for experimental music and s
 ound art)\nLocation: Brussels\, Belgium\; 10 residencies for international
  artists and 10 for artists living in Belgium.\nAward: NO artist fee. Inte
 rnational residents: shared accommodation in the Q-O2 apartment plus a tra
 vel contribution up to EUR 200. A small subsistence budget is reserved for
  artists who do not come with other funding. Work studio\, materials and t
 echnical equipment provided. No application fee.\nDuration: Usually 3 to 6
  weeks (international applicants: 4 to 6 weeks\; stays over 4 weeks not gu
 aranteed)\n\nMore: https://www.q-o2.be/en/in-residency/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.q-o2.be/en/in-residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Brussels\, Belgium\; 10 residencies for international artists and 
 10 for artists living in Belgium.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:icst-artists-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: ICST: Artists in Residence 2027 Open Call (ZHdK\, Zurich)
DESCRIPTION:The Institute for Computer Music and Sound Technology (ICST) at
  the Zurich University of the Arts (ZHdK) invites applications for its 202
 7 Artists in Residence program\, fostering artistic exchange in key areas 
 of current research. Residencies are available in five themes: Spatial Aud
 io\; Klavierautomat (algorithmic composition)\; Moving Loudspeakers\; Danc
 e and Generative AI\; and Object Performance. The program offers access to
  ICST's facilities and technical infrastructure\, professional support fro
 m researchers\, and per diems for meals and accommodation. Artists and mus
 icians working with sound and sound media\, whose practice reflects a stro
 ng interest in one of the listed research areas\, are encouraged to apply.
  One selected project from the Spatial Audio Residency will be featured at
  the SONIC MATTER Festival 2028 as part of an ongoing partnership. PRACTIC
 AL: residencies include use of facilities and technical infrastructure as 
 specified in the thematic descriptions\, plus technical support by ICST re
 search staff. Participants receive a contribution toward travel to Zurich 
 (up to CHF 300 for persons living in Europe\, up to CHF 500 for persons li
 ving outside Europe) and a per diem to cover meals and accommodation in Zu
 rich\; participants organise their own travel and accommodation\, with ICS
 T assistance if required. Residency dates are defined individually. APPLIC
 ATION: submitted via the online form\, uploading a concept sketch\, compos
 ition idea or project draft (PDF\, 2 pages\, 10 MB max)\; a portfolio of t
 hree selected works relevant to the residency topic including links to ext
 ernal audio and video (PDF\, 2 pages\, 10 MB max)\; and a tabular CV cover
 ing education and career (PDF\, 1 page\, 10 MB max). The residencies are a
 warded by a jury of ICST researchers and project leaders. TIMELINE: deadli
 ne 1 September 2026 at 24:00 CET\; candidates notified mid-October 2026. S
 elected candidates receive forms required for an invitation to Switzerland
  and must confirm participation and return completed forms within 10 days 
 or the invitation may be withdrawn.\n\nOrganisation: Institute for Compute
 r Music and Sound Technology (ICST)\, Zurich University of the Arts (ZHdK)
 \nLocation: Zurich\, Switzerland (in-person residency at ICST)\nAward: Use
  of ICST facilities and technical infrastructure plus technical support by
  research staff\; per diems for meals and accommodation during the residen
 cy\; travel contribution toward travel to Zurich (up to CHF 300 for person
 s living in Europe\, up to CHF 500 for those outside Europe). Participants
  organise their own travel and accommodation (ICST assists if required). N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Residency dates defined individually with se
 lected candidates\n\nMore: https://www.zhdk.ch/en/research/icst/icst-air/c
 onditions-selection-process-20736?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
URL:https://www.zhdk.ch/en/research/icst/icst-air/conditions-selection-proc
 ess-20736?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zurich\, Switzerland (in-person residency at ICST)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:zkm-hertzlab-sonic-experiments-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260628
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260629
SUMMARY:Deadline: ZKM | Hertzlab: Sonic Experiments 2026 - Resonating Futur
 es (Artist Residency)
DESCRIPTION:ZKM | Hertzlab's Sonic Experiments artist-in-residence programm
 e awards four scholarships to composers and sound artists specialising in 
 electronic music: three to international artists and one to a composer wit
 h a local connection to Karlsruhe (current/former address\, school\, unive
 rsity\, etc.). The 2026 edition\, 'Resonating Futures'\, seeks artists exp
 loring science fiction and space travel through composition and conceptual
  work\; thematic areas may include utopian and/or dystopian approaches\, t
 he global climate crisis\, decolonial perspectives\, health and wellbeing\
 , and the post-human world. The call is open to composers and sound artist
 s of all ages and backgrounds. PROJECT AREAS: composition for live electro
 nics\; mixed music (acoustic instruments combined with electronics)\; expe
 rimental performance with a prominent electronic-music or sound component\
 ; live coding\; and fixed media. Works may be produced in audiovisual form
 at\, and there is the opportunity to work with spatial sound (including fo
 r applicants new to it). FINANCIAL: EUR 1\,500 for the entire residency (c
 overs production\, living and travel)\, plus free ZKM accommodation near S
 chlosspark for non-local grantees. TO APPLY: submit application materials 
 to image@zkm.de by 28 June 2026\, 11:59pm CEST\; include the keywords 'Kar
 lsruhe local connection' in the subject line if applying for the local sch
 olarship. Incomplete or non-compliant applications will not be considered.
  Results announced July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: ZKM | Center for Art and Me
 dia Karlsruhe (Hertzlab)\nLocation: Karlsruhe\, Germany (free accommodatio
 n provided near Schlosspark)\nAward: EUR 1\,500 scholarship for the full r
 esidency\, from which grantees cover all production\, living and travel co
 sts. ZKM provides free accommodation near Karlsruhe Schlosspark (not provi
 ded for applicants already resident in Karlsruhe). No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Residency in 2026\n\nMore: https://zkm.de/en/open-call-sonic-exper
 iments-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://zkm.de/en/open-call-sonic-experiments-2026?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Karlsruhe\, Germany (free accommodation provided near Schlosspark)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:siirtymä-ambient-festival-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260701
SUMMARY:Deadline: Siirtymä Ambient Music Festival 2026: Open Call (Tampere
 \, Finland)
DESCRIPTION:Siirtymä Ambient Music Festival 2026 is a free\, community-dri
 ven festival in Tampere\, Finland\, organised by Suomen Ambientyhdistys ry
  (Finnish Ambient Association). The festival uses overlapping simultaneous
  performances across multiple locations\, emphasising spatial and ambient 
 experience over traditional stage formats. Open to artists and collectives
  working in ambient music\, sound art\, spatial installations\, and interd
 isciplinary practices\; no career-stage restriction\; the festival priorit
 ises emerging and lesser-known artists. The 2026 theme focuses on strength
 ening diversity\, creating multiple voices\, and finding new ways to encou
 nter one another and the urban environment. Technical support is provided 
 to selected participants. No travel or accommodation funding is publicly c
 onfirmed. NOTE: deadline of June 30 is from the Community Arts Network PDF
 \; verify at https://siirtyma.com/en/siirtym-2026 before submitting. Conta
 ct Suomen Ambientyhdistys ry directly for application details.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Suomen Ambientyhdistys ry (Finnish Ambient Association)\nLocation: T
 ampere\, Finland (multiple simultaneous venues\, site-specific)\nAward: Te
 chnical support provided. No artist fee publicly confirmed. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Festival date: 5 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://siirtym
 a.com/en/siirtym-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://siirtyma.com/en/siirtym-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tampere\, Finland (multiple simultaneous venues\, site-specific)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-creation-production-contemporary-music-2026@artificialnouve
 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creation and Production: Contemporary Music
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's creation and production grant for contemporary m
 usic supports the creation and production of new musical works\, including
  commissioned compositions\, music theatre\, sound installations\, and con
 temporary productions. Open to nationally established music professionals 
 and ensembles from Switzerland working in contemporary music\, music theat
 re\, sound art\, or contemporary folk music\, with prior Pro Helvetia supp
 ort. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\
 , or permanent residency with regular artistic activity in Switzerland)\; 
 not open to practitioners without a Swiss connection. AMOUNT: maximum CHF 
 25\,000\, depending on overall project size. Deadlines twice a year: 1 Mar
 ch (23:59 CET) and 1 September (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia po
 rtal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro Helvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Nation
 ally established Switzerland-based professionals and ensembles in contempo
 rary music\, music theatre\, sound art\, or contemporary folk.\nAward: Max
 imum CHF 25\,000 (depending on overall project size). No application fee.\
 nDuration: Creation/production of new works\; deadlines twice yearly (1 Ma
 rch and 1 September).\n\nMore: https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/crea
 tion-and-production-contemporary-music?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/creation-and-production-contempo
 rary-music?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nationally established Switzerland-based professionals and ensembl
 es in contemporary music\, music theatre\, sound art\, or contemporary fol
 k.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:national-gallery-iceland-cusp-residency-reykjavik-2027@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:Deadline: National Gallery of Iceland: CUSP Artist Residency (Reykj
 avik 2027)
DESCRIPTION:The National Gallery of Iceland announces an artist residency o
 pen call under its CUSP program\, a European cooperation project funded th
 rough Creative Europe's Culture grant. Artists working in complex media or
  emerging technologies (e.g. generative AI\, custom sensors\, sound\, soft
 ware-based\, blockchain\, physical and digital hybrid) are invited to appl
 y. This is the first of four residency stays offered to different artists 
 through the program\, one in each of the participating countries (Iceland\
 , Norway\, Czechia\, and Ukraine)\, followed by two micro residencies in t
 he Netherlands and Iceland. The programme brings together artists working 
 in time-based media with museum professionals\, conservators\, and technol
 ogy specialists developing preservation and conservation methodologies to 
 ensure the long-term endurance of artworks. The selected artist will meet 
 with a preservation specialist or conservator specializing in time-based m
 edia art for an in-depth artist interview addressing the preservation need
 s of their medium\, and will present their body of work and working method
 s publicly during an open-lab masterclass designed in collaboration with t
 he museum. RESIDENCY: up to four weeks in early 2027 in Reykjavik\, exact 
 dates arranged with the selected artist. WHAT IS PROVIDED: accommodation a
 nd working space\; a travel and subsistence stipend\; an artist fee for th
 e open lab/masterclass\; and possibly hardware and software depending on t
 he artist's request and museum means. ELIGIBILITY: international artists b
 ased outside Iceland\; applicants must be residents of any of the 27 EU me
 mber states or of non-EU countries with association agreements (EFTA/EEA m
 embers\, acceding countries\, candidate countries\, and European Neighbour
 hood Policy countries). APPLICATION: complete the application form with fu
 ll name\, country of residence\, gender identity\, contact information\, a
 n artistic statement (max 2500 characters)\, a motivation letter (max 2500
  characters)\, a draft idea of the public workshop or masterclass (max 100
 0 characters)\, links to social media/professional websites\, and a CV and
  portfolio upload (max 10MB each). DEADLINE: 3 September 2026 at 23:59 GMT
 . ABOUT CUSP: Creative Understanding\, Saving and Preserving Time-Based Me
 dia Art is a transnational cooperation project co-funded by the EU's Creat
 ive Europe Culture grant\, led by the National Gallery of Iceland with Nas
 jonalmuseet (Norway)\, LI-MA (Netherlands)\, Vasulka Kitchen (Czechia)\, a
 nd Mystetskyi Art Arsenal (Ukraine)\, focused on preserving and presenting
  time-based media art. Inquiries: cusp.residency.is [at] gmail.com.\n\nOrg
 anisation: National Gallery of Iceland (Listasafn Islands)\, CUSP project\
 nLocation: Reykjavik\, Iceland. Residency hosted by the National Gallery o
 f Iceland.\nAward: Accommodation and working space for the residency\; tra
 vel and subsistence stipend\; an artist fee for collaborating in the open-
 lab/masterclass\; and\, depending on the artist's request and museum means
 \, hardware and software for the working space. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Up to four weeks\, taking place in early 2027\, with exact dates arra
 nged with the selected artist.\n\nMore: https://www.listasafn.is/en/art/ne
 ws-vasulka-stofa/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://www.listasafn.is/en/art/news-vasulka-stofa/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Reykjavik\, Iceland. Residency hosted by the National Gallery of I
 celand.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ctm-2027-radio-lab-in-listening@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: In Listening 2027: Call for Hybrid Radio/Live Works (CTM 
 Festival\, Berlin)
DESCRIPTION:In Listening is the renamed successor to the CTM Radio Lab\, af
 ter more than a decade of collaboration between CTM Festival and Germany's
  public radio Deutschlandfunk Kultur\, with support from Austria's ORF\, z
 eroing in on sound-focused experiences. This open call is for works strong
 ly grounded in experimental sound practices and audio art and driven by co
 nceptual approaches or sonic narratives\, exploring the blurred edges betw
 een sound\, noise\, music\, storytelling\, poetry\, and documenting\, wher
 e sound is the main medium. Works should respond to the CTM 2027 theme 'Pr
 ocess...ing'\, with active listening informing the proposals. Applications
  should describe how the work could be developed for two complementary out
 puts: a LIVE EVENT at CTM 2027 and a RADIO BROADCAST on Deutschlandfunk Ku
 ltur and Oe1/ORF. At CTM\, works are presented in the silent green Kuppelh
 alle with an intimate setup\, the audience seated around the performer(s) 
 and surrounded by a 6.1-channel PA (creative use of fewer channels\, stere
 o\, or mono is welcome\; minimal lighting and scenography or performances 
 in the dark are suitable\, but video and complex scenography are out of sc
 ope). For radio/podcast\, proposals should consider the individual listeni
 ng experience (a recording of the performance is not sufficient)\; the bro
 adcast is a 40-55 minute piece aired in a late-night slot to a largely Ger
 man-speaking\, non-specialist audience. Works premiere at CTM 2027 (22-31 
 January 2027\, Berlin)\, are broadcast in Deutschlandfunk Kultur's Klangku
 nst programme in Spring 2027\, and presented via ORF (Oe1 Zeit-Ton or Blau
 e Stunde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotokoll im steirischen herbst in 
 Graz (Autumn 2027)\, then available for streaming for at least one year. B
 UDGET: two selected works each receive EUR 6\,000\; winners give up to two
  performances at CTM. Group proposals are possible but should keep a modes
 t travel budget. JURY: Jan Rohlf (CTM)\, Marcus Gammel (Deutschlandfunk Ku
 ltur)\, Anna Soucek (ORF Oe1)\, and one independent artist. TIMELINE: dead
 line 6 September 2026 at 23:59 Berlin time\; winners announced mid-October
  2026\; remote production late October 2026 to January 2027. APPLY (in Eng
 lish\, PDF\, max 20MB) with a project description including rough budget (
 max 4 pages)\, technical requirements\, and CV\; questions to in_listening
 @ctm-festival.de. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: CTM Festival with D
 eutschlandfunk Kultur and ORF\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. Premiered at CT
 M 2027 and broadcast on Deutschlandfunk Kultur\, with onward presentation 
 via ORF Oe1 (Zeit-Ton or Blaue Stunde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotok
 oll im steirischen herbst in Graz. Applications accepted internationally\,
  submitted in English.\nAward: Two selected works are each supported by a 
 fee of EUR 6\,000. CTM covers travel to Berlin and lodging during the prod
 uction and festival periods\; technical and staging costs for the CTM pres
 entation (and possible ORF musikprotokoll presentation) are covered separa
 tely by arrangement. Research\, creation and collaborator costs are the ar
 tist's own. Radio-production support (translations\, voiceovers\, studio t
 ime) can be provided by Deutschlandfunk Kultur upon discussion. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Work premiered at CTM Festival 22-31 January 2027\; r
 adio broadcast Spring 2027\; ORF/musikprotokoll presentation Autumn 2027. 
 Remote production phase late October 2026 to January 2027.\n\nMore: https:
 //www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/in-listening-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/in-listening-2027?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. Premiered at CTM 2027 and broadcast on Deutschla
 ndfunk Kultur\, with onward presentation via ORF Oe1 (Zeit-Ton or Blaue St
 unde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotokoll im steirischen herbst in Graz
 . Applications accepted internationally\, submitted in English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:columbia-ideas-imagination-paris-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T170454Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Columbia Institute for Ideas and Imagination: Paris Fello
 wship 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:Columbia University's Institute for Ideas and Imagination bring
 s a cohort of scholars and artists to Reid Hall in Paris for an academic y
 ear (September 2027 to May 2028)\, with a USD 75\,000 stipend\, housing\, 
 and research support. The creative-arts category explicitly includes visua
 l and sound arts and film alongside writing and composition. ELIGIBILITY: 
 any nationality\, but artists must not be permanently residentent in the U
 nited States (Netherlands-based artists qualify). Deadline 30 September 20
 26.\n\nOrganisation: Columbia University Institute for Ideas and Imaginati
 on\nLocation: Paris\, France (Reid Hall). Any nationality\; artists must N
 OT be permanently resident in the United States.\nAward: USD 75\,000 stipe
 nd\, plus housing at Reid Hall in Paris and office and research support\, 
 September 2027 to May 2028. No application fee.\nDuration: Fellowship year
  September 2027 to May 2028 at Reid Hall\, Paris.\n\nMore: https://ideasim
 agination.columbia.edu/apply/applying-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
